* Week 7: an unanchored 'A' | 'B' pattern is tried at every position in
* turn; at each one, both alternatives are tried before the cursor moves
* on at all (research/snobol/03-pattern-matching.md, "Pattern
* construction operators" and "matching is inherently unanchored"). Run
* with --trace to watch the history list record the untried alternative
* at each position and resume it before the cursor advances -- the match
* found is the earliest position where *either* alternative succeeds,
* even though 'A' occurs later in the subject than 'B' does.
        SUBJECT = 'ZZBA'
        SUBJECT 'A' | 'B'      :F(NOMATCH)
        OUTPUT = 'MATCHED'     :(STOP)
NOMATCH OUTPUT = 'NO MATCH'
STOP    SUBJECT = SUBJECT
